body.is-touch #health-panel { bottom: 158px; }
body.is-touch #weapon-panel { bottom: 158px; }
```
In the screenshot, the health panel is at y~650, which is bottom 160px, and weapon panel at y~680, overlapping because the health panel is 190px wide from left and weapon panel 150px from right on a 390px screen; total 340 + margins 24 = 364, leaves 26px gap. They shouldn't overlap horizontally, but the message is centered at bottom 118px, which is below them (y~715) and overlaps the joystick area. In the screenshot, the "Экипаж: экипаж занят" message is at y~715, over the touch area. The weapon panel text is at y~680, fine. The health panel left at y~650, fine. The message at y~715 overlaps the joystick? The joystick is at bottom left ~730, and the message is centered, so it overlaps the fire button area? The fire button is bottom right ~770. The message is above them, but it's in the middle. It's not terrible. But "Экипаж: экипаж занят" is a HUD message that appears during gameplay; it's centered and can overlap. We can move the mobile message to top center (below compass) to avoid controls:
```
@media (max-width: 820px) {
 #message { bottom: auto; top: 120px; font-size: 12px; }
 #prompt { bottom: auto; top: 150px; }
 #vehicle-panel { bottom: auto; top: 100px; }
}
```
But the top center has compass and killfeed/minimap. The message at top 120 would be below compass (top 18-40) and above center. Good. The prompt at top 150. Vehicle panel maybe top 100. For mobile, moving message to top is better. Let's adjust.

Also, the mobile screenshot shows a huge black mountain. Fix that first.

Also the HUD minimap overlaps the top-left sector? On mobile, minimap at right top, sector panel left top; fine.

The mobile crosshair is at center; good.

The mobile joystick is bottom left, fire button bottom right, use/reload/jump small buttons around right middle. Looks okay. The health/ammo panels are above the controls, good.

The black polygon is the biggest issue. Let's fix distant land material/placement. In `buildDistantLand`, use MeshBasicMaterial and move farther. Also maybe reduce count. Let's edit:
```
const mat = new THREE.MeshBasicMaterial({ color: 0x9a9276, fog: true });
...
const w = 90 + rng()*140, h = 14 + rng()*30;
...
g.position.set(-700 + i*175, -4, side*(520 + rng()*140));
```
But the world max z is ±320; distant land at ±520, beyond. Camera far 1600, visible. Fog at 520m: exp2 0.00135*520=0.702, squared 0.493, 1-exp(-0.493)=0.39 fog. Basic material with fog true blends toward fog color 0xbfb69b, so it will be hazy. Good. The cones will be smaller and farther, no giant black shape.

Alternatively, remove them entirely; the sky and terrain horizon is enough. But distant mountains add depth. Keep with hazy color.

Also, the black shape in the mobile screenshot might be a cloud sprite? Cloud sprites use a soft puff texture, white, opacity 0.18-0.48; not black. So it's the mountain.

Let's edit.

