content.text:
There's a bug in cloud opacity logic: I set opacity twice and baseOpacity may capture after modification. Let me simplify. Replace lines:
```js
c.material.opacity = (0.18 + night * 0.05) + (c.userData.baseOpacity ?? (c.userData.baseOpacity = c.material.opacity));
c.material.opacity = c.userData.baseOpacity * (1 - night * 0.65);
```
with:
```js
if (c.userData.baseOpacity === undefined) c.userData.baseOpacity = c.material.opacity;
c.material.opacity = c.userData.baseOpacity * (1 - night * 0.6);
```
Also allocation of new THREE.Color per frame for hemi; fix with constants maybe okay but 60fps allocations. Use `.set()` on existing color? `this.hemi.color.copy(_colC.set(0x2b3550).lerp(_colD.set(0xb9c7d6), light))`. Need _colD. Simpler keep new Color allocations (2/frame) - minor. But code quality. Let's fix opacity.

