Now spawnInitial changes. Let's rewrite the whole function to remove static MGs and add engineers/assault squads and moved A7V. Need to preserve crews etc.

Current function lines 271-344. We'll replace for clarity.

New spawnInitial:

```js
spawnInitial() {
  const make = ...
  // line infantry (7 per team) + engineers
  for (let i=0;i<7;i++){ ... british ... role rifle; }
  // engineers 2 per team
  for (let i=0;i<2;i++){
    const x = -260 + i*220; ...
    const z = trenchZ(x,side) - side*(trenchWidth(x)-0.9);
    const s = make({x,z,team,variant...,role:'engineer'});
    s.aiRole='engineer'; s.homeX=x... s.engineerCd= 2+i*3;
  }
  ...
  // sentries 4 per side as before
  // advancing squads from rear
  for team of [-1,1]:
    for i<4:
      const x = (side<0?-430:430)+(rand-.5)*180; 
      const z = side*(150 + Math.random()*60);
      s=make(...); s.aiRole='assault'; s.assault=true; s.homeX=x; s.homeZ=z; s.patrolX=x; s.patrolZ=z; s.aiMoveTimer=0;
  // tanks ...
  // crews...
  // corpses...
  // planes...
  // pilots...
  // aerodrome guards...
}
```

But initial "line infantry" in trench plus advancing squads gives many soldiers. Count: 7+2 per team +4 sentries +4 assault = 17 per team + crews. That's 34+. Fine.

Replace function entirely using exact old text? It's long. I'll target specific chunks.

First remove MG block (lines 299-310) and change British/German loops count maybe keep 11? Let's simplify: keep loops 11 but they are in trench; add engineers separately, add assault. The user wants far units; augment.

Edit MG block: remove.

